e:["$","span",null,{"className":"eyebrow","children":"WHY TEST THIS?"}]
f:["$","p",null,{"children":"Does preparing the guidance help? Does checking the agent’s work against it add a further benefit?"}]
10:["$","div",null,{"className":"hypothesis-explanation","children":"A capable agent may already work out the right approach from the sources. Preparing guidance and consulting it takes time and money. The experiment tests whether these steps prevent enough mistakes to justify the effort."}]
11:["$","div",null,{"className":"hypothesis-foot","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"signal-dot"}],"Planned method · See Progress & findings for readiness and results."]}]
12:["$","section",null,{"id":"example","className":"section-block","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"section-heading","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"section-no","children":"01"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"eyebrow","children":"GUIDANCE FOR A SPECIFIC TASK"}],["$","h2",null,{"children":"What would the layer tell an agent?"}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"section-intro","children":"When an agent is given a task, it needs to understand how that task fits into the existing system. The layer should identify code the agent can reuse, explain which decisions constrain the change, and show where exceptions apply. The agent should be able to see the evidence behind each answer and whether it represents an approved decision, an observed pattern or a question that still needs review."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"section-intro","children":"The agent can consult the layer about a proposed approach: whether to extend an existing component, where new code belongs, or whether a change would cross a boundary the project has chosen to preserve. The answer should explain what is allowed and why, or identify the unresolved decision that needs an owner’s judgement. The agent uses those answers in its plan, which can then be checked against the relevant decisions before work proceeds."}],["$","$L19",null,{"children":["$","$L1a",null,{"id":"guidance-examples","title":"See examples of the guidance an agent could receive","summary":"How this applies to change history, conflicting documentation and questions the code cannot answer.","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"NetBox is an open-source application used to document network infrastructure, including devices and their connections. It is one of the four projects in this study."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"In the first example, an agent is asked to write code that renames a device in NetBox. The layer would draw its attention to a related requirement: the change history must preserve the old name as well as the new one. It would also explain when NetBox already handles that requirement, so the agent can choose the right approach."}],["$","$L1b",null,{}]]}]}]]}]
13:["$","section",null,{"className":"section-block","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"section-heading","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"section-no","children":"02"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"eyebrow","children":"THE IDEA BEHIND THE LAYER"}],["$","h2",null,{"children":"Turn project evidence into guidance for later work"}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"section-intro section-intro-wide","children":"The layer connects two cycles: one establishes the guidance; the other uses it during engineering work. Drafting and approval happen before that guidance can be used as an approved decision, but they are not repeated for every task."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"guidance-cycles","id":"guidance-cycles","children":[["$","section",null,{"className":"guidance-cycle","aria-labelledby":"preparation-cycle-title","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"eyebrow","children":"DRAFTING & APPROVAL CYCLE"}],["$","h3",null,{"id":"preparation-cycle-title","children":"Establish and maintain the guidance"}],["$","ol",null,{"className":"cycle-steps","children":[["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","h4",null,{"children":"Find the evidence"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Read the relevant code, documentation and recorded decisions, including exceptions and conflicting examples."}]]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","h4",null,{"children":"Draft and verify the guidance"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Explain each proposed rule, its scope and its evidence. Check support and contradictions before owner review."}]]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","h4",null,{"children":"Review and release a version"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"The responsible owner approves, rejects or requests changes. Only approved decisions are released as approved guidance."}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"cycle-repeat","children":[["$","$Ld",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":[["path",{"d":"M3 12a9 9 0 0 1 9-9 9.75 9.75 0 0 1 6.74 2.74L21 8","key":"v9h5vc"}],["path",{"d":"M21 3v5h-5","key":"1q7to0"}],["path",{"d":"M21 12a9 9 0 0 1-9 9 9.75 9.75 0 0 1-6.74-2.74L3 16","key":"3uifl3"}],["path",{"d":"M8 16H3v5","key":"1cv678"}]],"className":"lucide-refresh-cw","size":17,"aria-hidden":"true"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Review can send a draft back for revision before a version is released."}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"cycle-timing","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Initially:"}]," establish the baseline.",["$","br",null,{}],["$","strong",null,{"children":"When evidence or decisions change:"}]," recheck affected guidance and retain, revise or retire it through review."]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"guidance-connection","children":[["$","$Ld",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":[["path",{"d":"M5 12h14","key":"1ays0h"}],["path",{"d":"m12 5 7 7-7 7","key":"xquz4c"}]],"className":"lucide-arrow-right guidance-connection-arrow","size":28,"aria-hidden":"true"}],["$","strong",null,{"children":"Approved guidance"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"A version with its evidence, scope and exceptions."}],["$","span",null,{"children":"The same version can support many tasks."}]]}],["$","section",null,{"className":"guidance-cycle guidance-cycle-use","aria-labelledby":"usage-cycle-title","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"eyebrow","children":"USAGE CYCLE"}],["$","h3",null,{"id":"usage-cycle-title","children":"Apply the guidance to each task"}],["$","ol",null,{"className":"cycle-steps","children":[["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","h4",null,{"children":"Consult and plan"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Retrieve the relevant guidance. Identify what can be reused, what constrains the change and which exceptions may apply."}]]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","h4",null,{"children":"Check and carry out the approach"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Review the plan against the guidance, make the change and recheck material changes of approach."}]]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","h4",null,{"children":"Check the resulting work"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Assess the change against the relevant decisions and task requirements. Record objections and unresolved questions."}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"cycle-repeat","children":[["$","$Ld",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":"$13:props:children:2:props:children:0:props:children:3:props:children:0:props:iconNode","className":"lucide-refresh-cw","size":17,"aria-hidden":"true"}],"$L1c"]}],"$L1d"]}],"$L1e"]}],"$L1f","$L20"]}]
14:["$","section",null,{"className":"section-block","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"section-heading","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"section-no","children":"03"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"eyebrow","children":"THE PROPOSED COMPARISON"}],["$","h2",null,{"children":"Separate the value of guidance from the value of checking its use"}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"section-intro","children":"The design compares agents making the same change under three conditions. This separates the effect of prepared guidance from the additional effect of consultation and checking. The two guidance groups receive the same frozen rules, and preparation costs are recorded. Prompts, budgets and checks are specified and validated before the trial."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"comparison comparison-three","children":[["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"eyebrow","children":"WITHOUT THE EXTRA LAYER"}],["$","h3",null,{"children":"The agent works from the sources"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"It searches the code and available documentation, works out what matters for the task, and makes the change. This represents a capable agent doing the work directly."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"eyebrow","children":"WITH PREPARED GUIDANCE"}],["$","h3",null,{"children":"The agent receives the rules"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"The layer has examined the same sources and written guidance before the task begins. The agent receives that guidance and works with it, without an interactive check by the layer."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"eyebrow","children":"WITH GUIDANCE AND INTERACTION"}],["$","h3",null,{"children":"The agent checks its proposed actions"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"The agent receives the same guidance, consults the layer about its plan and responds to checks at agreed points. The run records whether those interactions prevent mistakes or add unnecessary work."}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"review-comparison","id":"review-comparison","children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Every group gets a review"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"All three groups have their plans and code reviewed at the same points, with the same number of opportunities to make corrections. What differs is the help available during review:"}],["$","table",null,{"className":"review-comparison-table","children":[["$","caption",null,{"className":"sr-only","children":"What the reviewer checks in each group"}],["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","th",null,{"scope":"col","children":"Group"}],["$","th",null,{"scope":"col","children":"What the reviewer checks"}]]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","th",null,{"scope":"row","children":"Sources only"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"The plan and code against the available sources, including the project’s actual AGENTS.md instructions."}]]}],["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","th",null,{"scope":"row","children":"Prepared guidance"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"The same, with the prepared guidance also available."}]]}],["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","th",null,{"scope":"row","children":"Guidance and interaction"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"The same, plus targeted questions about which rules apply, how the proposed change follows them, and whether an exception is justified."}]]}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"children":"This tests whether structured questioning improves the result beyond an ordinary review with guidance available. Every group has the same overall resource limit, and all review effort counts towards it."}]]}]]}]
15:["$","section",null,{"className":"section-block","id":"method","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"section-heading","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"section-no","children":"04"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"eyebrow","children":"THE EXPERIMENT, STEP BY STEP"}],["$","h2",null,{"children":"How the experiment is designed to run"}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"section-intro","children":"The experiment will ask agents to make the same code change with different kinds of help, then compare the work they produce and the effort it took. Here is the proposed sequence for one test."}],["$","ol",null,{"className":"method-steps","aria-label":"The four steps in one experiment","children":[["$","li",null,{"className":"method-step","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"method-step-heading","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"method-step-number","aria-hidden":"true","children":"1"}],["$","h3",null,{"children":"Prepare a task with a defensible assessment"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"method-step-content","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"For each backtest, case preparation records the task, the historical implementation and the guardrails that applied to that work. Before an agent attempts it, the assessment establishes the required behaviour, relevant rules and legitimate exceptions. The historical solution and its assessment stay outside the agent’s workspace."}],["$","$L19",null,{"children":["$","$L1a",null,{"id":"choose-case","title":"How are tasks selected and assessment criteria established?","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Start with the evidence."}]," Each case uses a published requirement or decision. Its scope is checked against the code, and any disagreement is recorded. Neither the documentation nor the implementation is assumed to be correct."]}],["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Check that the assessment can tell the difference."}]," Each case includes:"]}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"plain-list","children":[["$","li",null,{"children":"A valid solution."}],["$","li",null,{"children":"A deliberately incorrect change."}],["$","li",null,{"children":"A legitimate exception or alternative."}]]}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Tests must distinguish these outcomes. Where the evidence cannot settle a judgement, it remains unresolved."}],["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Keep the coverage in perspective."}]," The candidate projects are NetBox, Wagtail, Paperless-ngx and HTTPX. They cover different engineering decisions, but all use Python and three use Django. Findings from these projects cannot represent all software development."]}],["$","$L21",null,{}]]}]}]]}]]}],["$","li",null,{"className":"method-step","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"method-step-heading","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"method-step-number","aria-hidden":"true","children":"2"}],["$","h3",null,{"children":"Let the layer prepare its guidance"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"method-step-content","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"The layer examines the allowed project material without seeing the change task. It drafts guidance, and a separate verifier checks whether the evidence supports it. The resulting guide is saved before the task is revealed and stays unchanged during the run."}],["$","$L19",null,{"children":[["$","$L1a",null,{"id":"allowed-evidence","title":"Does the layer read the documentation, or work the rule out from code?","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":["The experiment tests those two abilities separately. Each project’s actual ",["$","code",null,{"children":"AGENTS.md"}]," files, including applicable directory-specific instructions, are supplied from the starting revision to all three groups. If those instructions state a tested rule, the case is classified as using documented guidance. Missing files are recorded as absent."]}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"plain-list","children":["$L22","$L23"]}],"$L24","$L25"]}],"$L26"]}]]}]]}],"$L27","$L28"]}],"$L29","$L2a"]}]
16:["$","section",null,{"className":"section-block","id":"technical-setup","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"section-heading","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"section-no","children":"05"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"eyebrow","children":"TECHNICAL SETUP"}],["$","h2",null,{"children":"How the components work together"}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"section-intro","children":"A runner coordinates the experiment. It supplies each agent with its permitted inputs, passes review messages between roles, controls code execution and records the results. Agents receive separate working environments; the runner controls the connections between them."}],["$","figure",null,{"className":"technical-diagram","aria-labelledby":"technical-diagram-caption","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"technical-flow","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"technical-node","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"eyebrow","children":"INPUTS"}],["$","h3",null,{"children":"Prepared input packs"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Pinned source files, applicable project instructions and each role’s permitted task material."}]]}],["$","$Ld",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":"$13:props:children:2:props:children:1:props:children:0:props:iconNode","className":"lucide-arrow-right technical-arrow","aria-hidden":"true"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"technical-node technical-controller","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"eyebrow","children":"OUTSIDE AGENT CONTROL"}],["$","h3",null,{"children":"Runner and controller"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Dispatch inputs, validate exchanges, enforce checkpoints and stop decisions, and record activity."}]]}],["$","$Ld",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":[["path",{"d":"M8 3 4 7l4 4","key":"9rb6wj"}],["path",{"d":"M4 7h16","key":"6tx8e3"}],["path",{"d":"m16 21 4-4-4-4","key":"siv7j2"}],["path",{"d":"M20 17H4","key":"h6l3hr"}]],"className":"lucide-arrow-left-right technical-arrow","aria-hidden":"true"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"technical-node","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"eyebrow","children":"SEPARATE ENVIRONMENTS"}],["$","h3",null,{"children":"Agent roles and code execution"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Each role receives its own context and workspace. Generated code executes in a restricted test environment."}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"technical-handoff","children":[["$","$Ld",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":"$1:3:props:children:1:props:children:0:props:children:4:props:children:0:props:children:1:props:iconNode","className":"lucide-arrow-down","aria-hidden":"true"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"After the attempt stops: final artifacts and recorded observations pass to evaluation."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"technical-evaluation","children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Independent evaluation"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"The evaluator receives the final code and separately held assessment criteria. Historical and agent implementations are assessed under the same rules. Final scores and hidden-test feedback do not return to the running agents."}]]}],["$","figcaption",null,{"id":"technical-diagram-caption","children":"Planned data flow. Arrows represent permitted transfers through the runner; they do not imply shared agent storage or unrestricted connections."}]]}],["$","$L19",null,{"children":[["$","$L1a",null,{"id":"technical-inputs","title":"What does each role receive?","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"Each input pack has a manifest: a list of permitted files with hashes that identify their exact contents. The runner checks the manifest before dispatch and starts a fresh context for each role and run."}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"plain-list","children":[["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Drafter and verifier:"}]," the permitted project evidence and instructions. The verifier also receives the proposed claims. Neither receives the later change task or final assessment."]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Coder and reviewer:"}]," the task, permitted sources and applicable project instructions. GUIDE and INTERACT also receive the same frozen generated guidance. Reviewers receive the submitted plan and changes; they do not receive the coder’s private reasoning."]}],"$L2b"]}],"$L2c"]}],"$L2d","$L2e","$L2f"]}],"$L30"]}]
17:["$","div",null,{"className":"route-footer","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"For the work completed so far and the decisions still ahead."}],["$","a",null,{"href":"/interpretation-layer-poc/progress/","children":["Progress & findings ",["$","$Ld",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":"$13:props:children:2:props:children:1:props:children:0:props:iconNode","className":"lucide-arrow-right","size":18}]]}]]}]
18:["$","footer",null,{"className":"site-footer","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"AI Engineering Playbook · Interpretation-layer validation"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Research in progress · Updated as the study develops"}]]}]
1c:["$","span",null,{"children":"Objections can send the plan or code back for revision, or stop the attempt."}]
1d:["$","p",null,{"className":"cycle-timing","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"For each task:"}]," use the applicable guidance without reopening every approved decision."]}]
1e:["$","div",null,{"className":"guidance-feedback","children":[["$","$Ld",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":[["path",{"d":"M20 20v-7a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H4","key":"1nkjon"}],["path",{"d":"M9 14 4 9l5-5","key":"102s5s"}]],"className":"lucide-corner-up-left","size":21,"aria-hidden":"true"}],["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"New evidence can prompt a guidance review."}]," Work may expose an outdated rule, a conflict or an unrecorded exception. Send that evidence back to the drafting and approval cycle; it does not automatically change an approved decision."]}]]}]
1f:["$","div",null,{"className":"scope-note","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"What this POC can test"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"The first POC is designed as a self-contained experiment to minimise dependencies on project maintainers, organisational approvals and ongoing operational involvement. Public code and recorded decisions provide a basis for testing whether guidance is supported by evidence and helps with later work."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"This limits the claim: evidence verification does not establish owner approval, and a fixed guidance version does not test ongoing maintenance. Later iterations could involve project owners and examine maintenance if these are needed to answer the remaining questions."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"The diagram above describes the full proposal. This pilot freezes guidance before each matched comparison; feedback from final evaluation cannot be used to repair it during a run."}]]}]]}]
20:["$","div",null,{"className":"working-loop","children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"How agent review is designed to work in this POC"}],["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Planned review procedure."}]," In the interactive condition, a separate checking agent would assess the coding agent’s proposed approach and its resulting changes. It would use the same permitted evidence and the guidance prepared before the task, without access to the withheld assessment."]}],["$","ol",null,{"className":"numbered-detail","children":[["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Check the plan before the first edit."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"The coding agent asks the layer what to reuse and which rules apply. It then submits the components it will change, the rules it will follow and any exception it intends to use. The checker assesses that reasoning, rather than merely looking for citations."}]]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Make objections lead to a recorded decision."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"The checker returns “proceed”, “revise” or “unresolved”, with a reason. A request to revise goes back to the coding agent. The pilot proposal allows at most two correction rounds per checkpoint; an unresolved decision or an exhausted allowance stops the attempt and is recorded for later assessment."}]]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Check a changed approach before work continues."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"If the agent needs a new dependency, changes the component it plans to reuse, or relies on a new exception, it must submit an updated plan. The program running the experiment would also compare each submitted code change with the plan. A mismatch sends the attempt back for review."}]]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Judge the code independently at the end."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"All conditions run the same task checks. In each backtest, a separate evaluator assesses both the agent’s change and the historical implementation for task correctness and compliance with the applicable guardrails. If the agent avoids a violation in the historical code while completing the task correctly, that counts in its favour. Matching the original code is not the goal."}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"caption","children":"Owner approval of new decisions, renewal of guidance and checks across an organisation’s systems remain outside this pilot."}]]}]
22:["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Working it out from code."}]," Eligible cases do not state the target rule in their applicable AGENTS.md instructions. Other narrative disclosures are withheld consistently across the matched groups. The layer uses the remaining code evidence, or acknowledges that the rule cannot be established."]}]
23:["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Using documentation."}]," The declared documents are available. The assessment checks whether the layer understands their scope, preserves exceptions and notices disagreements with the code."]}]
24:["$","p",null,{"children":"Each claim must say where it came from. A rule copied from a guide will not be reported as a rule inferred from code. The verifier uses only the material allowed in that test; it cannot consult the hidden assessment to repair the guide."}]
25:["$","p",null,{"children":"Missing or incorrect guidance remains part of the result. The assessment also covers unsupported claims and whether the layer recognises uncertainty. The website’s examples are illustrations, not the guidance supplied to an experimental agent."}]
26:["$","$L1a",null,{"id":"isolation","title":"How is withheld assessment material kept out of the inputs?","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":["Each role receives only its permitted input pack. Historical solutions and final assessment material stay outside coding and runtime-review environments. The ",["$","a",null,{"className":"text-link","href":"#technical-setup","children":"technical setup"}]," explains the execution boundaries and permitted communication routes."]}],["$","p",null,{"children":"The input audit must also look for disclosures in comments, tests, examples and dependencies. Removing the obvious guide does not establish that its contents have been withheld."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Public code may already be familiar to a model from training. Some tests will therefore use unpublished changes that alter the correct rule. The assessment checks whether the answer follows the changed code. Harmless renaming should leave the interpretation unchanged. These controls can make the test inspectable; they cannot prove that the original project was absent from training data."}]]}]
27:["$","li",null,{"className":"method-step","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"method-step-heading","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"method-step-number","aria-hidden":"true","children":"3"}],["$","h3",null,{"children":"Run the same task three ways"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"method-step-content","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"Separate agent attempts receive the same task and the same allowed project sources. What changes is the help they receive:"}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"method-groups","children":[["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Sources only."}]," The agent works out what matters from the code and available documentation."]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Sources and guidance."}]," The agent also receives the guide prepared in step 2."]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Sources, guidance and interaction."}]," The agent receives that same guide and consults the layer about its plan and actions."]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"children":"All three groups get ordinary review and opportunities to correct mistakes. The interactive group also receives targeted questions about how it applies the rules. The required review points and correction limits are the same across groups, and all reviewing counts towards the agreed budget."}],["$","$L19",null,{"children":["$","$L1a",null,{"id":"during-work","title":"What does the checker do while the agent works?","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Before the first edit,"}]," the interactive agent consults the layer and submits a plan. It explains what it will reuse, what it will change and which rules or exceptions apply. A separate checker assesses whether those proposed actions follow the evidence."]}],["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"During implementation,"}]," the runner checks incoming code submissions against the approved plan. At the configured review points, and whenever a material change of approach is detected, it pauses further work and sends the plan and changes to the checker. The checker assesses the applicable rules and exceptions while the task is still in progress, so a blocking issue can be corrected before work continues."]}],["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"After a check,"}]," the agent receives “proceed”, “revise” or “unresolved”, with a reason. The proposed limit is two correction rounds at each required review point. An unresolved decision, or failure to satisfy the check within that allowance, stops the attempt. Unfinished work remains in the assessment."]}],["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"If the approach changes,"}]," a new dependency, a different component to reuse or a new claimed exception requires an updated plan. Tests must establish that the runner catches undeclared changes too. These in-run checks are triggered by submissions and detected changes; the checkpoint schedule and limits are defined before the run."]}],["$","p",null,{"children":"The checker can see the task, plan, changes and permitted evidence. It cannot see the hidden answers or the coding agent’s private reasoning. It cannot rewrite the frozen guidance. Questions needing an owner’s authority remain unresolved; the procedure does not permit an unrecorded human answer during a run."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Reviewers in the other groups can still identify mistakes and request corrections. They use their group’s sources and, where supplied, guidance. The intended difference is the structured consultation and targeted questions, not the mere presence of a reviewer. Instructions and budgets are specified and tested before runs."}]]}]}]]}]]}]
28:["$","li",null,{"className":"method-step","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"method-step-heading","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"method-step-number","aria-hidden":"true","children":"4"}],["$","h3",null,{"children":"Judge the finished work and compare the cost"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"method-step-content","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"A separate evaluator assesses both the historical implementation and the agent’s change using the same criteria prepared in step 1:"}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"plain-list","children":[["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Task correctness:"}]," does the implementation deliver the required behaviour?"]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Guardrail compliance:"}]," does it follow the applicable, evidence-supported rules and legitimate exceptions?"]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"children":"If the historical code violates a guardrail and the agent avoids that violation while completing the task correctly, the agent receives credit for the improvement. A different valid solution is not penalised for differing from the original. Points and weighting are fixed before scored runs."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Before any agent runs, each case has an assessment based on the project’s evidence. It defines what the task must achieve and which project rules apply. Every group and the historical implementation are assessed against those same criteria."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"The layer’s generated guidance is checked against that evidence too. A new rule proposed by the layer does not automatically become a requirement used to score the work."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Separate records show whether reviews raised unnecessary objections, whether the task was finished, and how much preparation and review cost."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"The first comparison tests whether prepared guidance helps. Comparing the two groups that receive guidance tests whether interaction adds a further benefit."}],["$","$L19",null,{"children":[["$","$L1a",null,{"id":"reliable-judge","title":"How will the judge’s reliability be established?","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"Each judging role—the verifier, runtime checker and final judge—must pass its own reliability test."}],["$","ol",null,{"className":"plain-list","children":[["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Develop the instructions."}]," Use examples whose expected assessments are supported by project requirements, documented rules and reproducible tests. The historical implementation is evidence to examine, and may itself contain mistakes; it does not define the correct answer."]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Set the pass criteria in advance."}]," Decide the acceptable error rates and how much validation evidence is needed before seeing the results."]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Test on fresh cases."}]," Freeze the instructions, then test them on different kinds of project decisions. Examples used to improve the judge cannot also prove its reliability."]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Measure its mistakes."}]," Count incorrect work it accepts and correct work it rejects separately. Check that it accepts valid exceptions and recognises insufficient evidence. Repeat grading and vary presentation to see whether irrelevant differences change its verdict."]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"children":"The judge does not see group labels or model names when scoring code. Review interactions are assessed separately."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"The expected assessment must rest on reproducible behaviour or clear project evidence, with independent expertise where needed. Agreement between two AI models is not enough. If the evidence cannot settle a judgement, it remains unresolved."}],"$L31","$L32"]}],"$L33"]}]]}]]}]
29:["$","div",null,{"className":"method-preparation","children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Validation precedes the main trial"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Component validation and a small pilot test the procedure before its results support conclusions. Findings from the pilot inform the method and size of the main trial."}],["$","a",null,{"className":"text-link","href":"/interpretation-layer-poc/progress/","children":["See preparation, decisions and results ",["$","$Ld",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":"$13:props:children:2:props:children:1:props:children:0:props:iconNode","className":"lucide-arrow-right","size":16}]]}]]}]
2a:["$","p",null,{"className":"caption","children":["The ",["$","a",null,{"className":"text-link","href":"/interpretation-layer-poc/evidence/working-poc-plan.md","download":true,"children":"working experiment plan"}]," records the full method and design decisions. The ",["$","a",null,{"className":"text-link","href":"/interpretation-layer-poc/progress/#evidence","children":"evidence record and case library"}]," are on Progress & findings."]}]
2b:["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Final judge:"}]," the code to assess, task requirements, guardrail criteria and independently produced test observations. Origin, treatment and model labels are withheld for individual code scoring."]}]
2c:["$","p",null,{"children":["The project’s actual ",["$","code",null,{"children":"AGENTS.md"}]," files, including applicable directory-specific instructions, are taken from the backtest’s starting revision. The same applicable files are supplied across all three groups. Their absence is recorded rather than filled with invented instructions. If they state a tested rule, that case is classified as using documented guidance."]}]
2d:["$","$L1a",null,{"id":"technical-execution","title":"How are plans, reviews and model calls coordinated?","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"The runner tracks the state of each attempt: awaiting a plan, awaiting review, permitted to work, awaiting a revision, or stopped. It accepts only exchanges allowed for that role and stage. A material change of approach returns the attempt to plan review. Unresolved decisions, exhausted limits and containment failures trigger the specified stop procedure."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"During implementation, incoming code submissions are checked against the approved plan. The runner pauses at configured review points and on detected material changes, then passes the relevant plan and code to the reviewer. Work resumes only after the required decision permits it. The same checkpoint opportunities and limits apply across all three groups."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"A model gateway makes the authorised model calls and records usage. Credentials remain outside the agent workspace. The controller passes only the required questions, submissions and decisions between roles; it does not expose a general command interface. Checking a message’s format does not establish that its content is trustworthy."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Candidate code runs separately from the controller and the full assessment store. Common task checks may return permitted feedback during work. Final evaluation uses a separate assessment path after the attempt ends."}]]}]
2e:["$","$L1a",null,{"id":"technical-isolation","title":"How is access beyond the test environment restricted?","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"The design requires agents to have no general access to the host machine, other runs or external services. The runner still needs narrowly defined routes to supply inputs, pass permitted review messages and collect outputs. Those interfaces are part of the isolation boundary and must be tested too."}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"plain-list","children":[["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Restrict and record communication."}]," Permitted exchanges pass through the external controller. Other routes must be blocked, including indirect communication through shared services."]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Minimise and test exposed services."}]," Each agent receives only the tools, storage and network capabilities its task requires. Every exposed capability is reviewed for unintended access. Preinstalled, read-only dependencies are one way to remove a live service from the execution environment."]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Protect the host and assessment."}]," Host files, credentials and administrative controls stay outside agent access. Workspaces and caches cannot provide shared writable channels. The controller, stop mechanism and assessment records remain protected from agent writes."]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Test attempted boundary crossings."}]," Controlled probes check file access, communication between roles and runs, direct and indirect network access, and attempts to alter enforcement. The relevant checks are repeated after environment changes. Detected failures stop affected runs and preserve the evidence."]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"children":["The Hugging Face incident demonstrated how a shared package service could become an unintended message board and a route to the internet. It motivates reviewing all exposed services, not only package installation. ",["$","a",null,{"className":"text-link","href":"https://openai.com/index/hugging-face-incident-and-the-road-ahead/","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer","children":"OpenAI’s account"}]," and ",["$","a",null,{"className":"text-link","href":"https://huggingface.co/blog/agent-intrusion-technical-timeline","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer","children":"Hugging Face’s technical account"}]," describe the incident."]}],["$","p",null,{"children":"The runner must record its isolation boundaries and the results of tests that attempt to cross them. These tests establish protection against the routes examined, with remaining limitations stated. They cannot guarantee that escape is impossible."}],["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Architecture choice to resolve:"}]," a disposable virtual machine around restricted execution is a candidate design. The isolation technology and controller interfaces must be selected and tested against these requirements; the diagram does not prescribe a specific platform."]}]]}]
2f:["$","$L1a",null,{"id":"technical-records","title":"What makes a run inspectable and repeatable?","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"Each run records the source revision, file manifests, environment version, model settings, exact supplied inputs and returned outputs, tool activity, review decisions, revisions, stops and resource use. An external audit store retains these records so an agent cannot rewrite its own history."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"The assessment records task correctness and guardrail compliance separately, including justified improvements over historical code, new violations and unresolved evidence. Public reports exclude credentials and sealed assessment material. Exact models, budgets, scoring weights and acceptance limits belong in the run configuration, fixed before the relevant scored runs."}]]}]
30:["$","p",null,{"className":"caption","children":["The method defines the required behaviour. ",["$","a",null,{"className":"text-link","href":"/interpretation-layer-poc/progress/#technical-status","children":"Progress & findings records component readiness and open technical choices."}]]}]
31:["$","p",null,{"children":"Scores are audited during the pilot. If the judge changes, it must pass validation again, and every affected group is rescored using the revised version."}]
32:["$","p",null,{"children":["Section 9A of the ",["$","a",null,{"className":"text-link","href":"/interpretation-layer-poc/evidence/working-poc-plan.md","download":true,"children":"working plan"}]," contains the full qualification procedure."]}]
33:["$","$L1a",null,{"id":"interpret-results","title":"What conclusions would the comparison support?","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"Useful guidance must be supported by evidence, improve later work and justify its cost. The guidance itself also needs assessment, so a correct code change does not conceal unsupported rules. A separate small diagnostic supplies a known rule directly to check whether the task could benefit from correct guidance at all."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Several tasks may test the same underlying decision. The analysis must account for that relationship rather than count every variation or repeated attempt as independent evidence. The number of cases and minimum worthwhile improvement are set before the main trial."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"A positive result would support the layer in the situations tested. It would not establish universal necessity, owner approval of new rules, adoption by a team or the value of keeping guidance current across an organisation. Inconclusive and negative results would also inform revisions to Chapter 4."}],["$","a",null,{"className":"text-link","href":"https://yspbob.github.io/AI-Playbook/AI_Engineering_Playbook.html#4-the-interpretation-layer","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer","children":["Read Chapter 4 in the public playbook ",["$","$Ld",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":"$1:1:props:children:props:children:1:props:children:1:props:iconNode","className":"lucide-arrow-up-right","size":16}]]}]]}]
